  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Amylopectin is insoluble in water and constitutes about 80-85% starch.<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/d88c93e4-df2a-4617-91aa-714f31d256ed-image25.png\" /></p><p>Amylopectin is a water-soluble polysaccharide and highly branched polymer of a-glucose units found in plants. It is one of the two components of starch, the other being amylose. Amylopectin bears a straight/linear chain along with a number of side chains which may be branched further.</p>",
